<h1 style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:800;">Conversion Tracking</h1>
<p>Track not just clicks, but actual conversions — leads and sales — attributed to each link.</p>

<h2>How It Works</h2>
<p>UTMPro tracks three types of events:</p>
<ul><li><strong>Clicks:</strong> Every time someone visits your short link</li><li><strong>Leads:</strong> When a visitor converts to a lead (form fill, sign-up)</li><li><strong>Sales:</strong> When a lead becomes a customer (purchase)</li></ul>

<h2>Setting Up Conversion Tracking</h2>
<p>Use the UTMPro API or webhooks to send conversion events back to UTMPro. Each event is attributed to the original link click using the visitor's tracking cookie.</p>

<h2>Viewing the Funnel</h2>
<p>On the link detail page, you'll see the full conversion funnel:</p>
<p style="text-align:center;font-size:1.5rem;">Clicks → Leads → Sales</p>
<p>This gives you a clear picture of which links drive real business results, not just traffic.</p>
